lj.
declare A,B:bool.
# Prove contraposition from a deleg A->B
#
# A-B is A/\~B, the counterexample shape for A->B, so refuting it is exactly
# the contrapositive ~B->~A.  Refuting X-Y asks for Y from X: elim puts the
# subtrahend in the conclusions and leaves a context goal for the minuend, so
# A-B asks for B from A, which the deleg A->B supplies.  (B-A would ask for A
# from B instead, which A->B does not give -- see the note at the end.)
counterargument contra : (A-B).
elim h.
cut (A->B) rule.
by default.
next.
elim.
axiom rule.
moxia h.
dixi.

# The remaining open goal is the deleg A->B itself, so the counterargument
# rests on that single default.
#
# For the mirrored conclusion B-A the deleg has to be mirrored too:
# start counterargument contra2 B-A
# elim h.
# cut (B->A) rule.
# by default.
# next.
# elim.
# axiom rule.
# moxia h.
# end counterargument
